grund.toml is read as version 1.

[scan] extensions
Values: array of strings
The file extensions the scan reads. The default is `md` plus every extension grund's built-in language table names, so a language grund learns is read without a config change. An empty string, which version 1 keeps for compatibility, also reads every file with no extension. Version 2 has no such entry and `grund config migrate` refuses it, so give such a file an extension instead.
